WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Welcome to our training on the Brand Analytics Search Query Performance Report.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Brands enrolled in Amazon Brand Registry enjoy access to a suite of additional selling benefits,

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.000
including the Brand Analytics tool in Seller Central.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.955
In this video, we'll review the features and functionality of one of the reports you'll find in

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:24.000
Brand Analytics, Search Query Performance.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.000
This report shows sellers how customers search for their brand in the Amazon store.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.000
It can help them understand the ways customers discover their products,

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.000
highlighting trends and opportunities to expand their product catalog.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:44.000
You can access the Search Query Performance Report and others in the Brand Analytics tool

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.000
if you're a seller internal to a brand enrolled in Brand Registry.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Simply select Brands in the main menu in Seller Central.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Then click Brand Analytics, or click All Brand Benefits, then locate the Brand Analytics card.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.000
For more information about accessing Brand Analytics and other Brand Registry tools,

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:12.000
see our modules in Seller University about requesting or managing access to brand selling benefits.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.588
When you access the Brand Analytics tool, you'll be brought directly to the Search Query Performance

00:01:18.588 --> 00:01:19.000
Report.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.000
You can access additional reports using the tabs at the top of the screen.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:30.000
The Search Query Performance Report lists customer queries associated with your brand's products.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.545
The most popular query will have the highest score and appear at the top, with all other queries

00:01:36.545 --> 00:01:38.000
in descending order below.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.000
Up to 1,000 queries are shown.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.000
Next to each query, you'll see a sequence of metrics.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:51.000
Search Query Volume is the number of times customers search the Amazon store using a query.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:57.000
For example, maybe customers searched using the phrase "water pitcher" 100 times.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Impressions is the number of products that appeared on Search Results pages after a query was used.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.000
It includes both organic and sponsored products.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.478
You'll see the total count or total number of product impressions, as well as a brand count and

00:02:12.478 --> 00:02:14.000
brand share for the query.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:19.000
Brand count is the number of product impressions specifically for your brand.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:25.000
Brand share is that same number divided by the total number of impressions for the query.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:32.500
For example, after customers used the query "water pitcher" 100 times, 1,000 products appeared on

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.000
Search Results pages.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:40.742
If 300 of those impressions were for a water pitcher that is part of your brand, the brand count

00:02:40.742 --> 00:02:45.000
listed would be 300 and the brand share listed would be 30%.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:51.667
Note that impressions don't include product appearances in widgets like those for highly rated products

00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:53.000
or new arrivals.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:59.400
Clicks is the number of times customers clicked products that appeared on Search Results pages after

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.000
a query was used.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:07.000
Like with impressions, you'll see a total count, brand count and brand share for clicks.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:13.000
You'll also see a column for same day shipping speed, which is the number of times products were

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.000
clicked while the same day shipping option was viewable.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.625
For example, if customers clicked various products 50 times after using the query "water pitcher"

00:03:21.625 --> 00:03:29.125
and 25 of those clicks were for your water pitcher, the brand count listed would be 25 and the brand

00:03:29.125 --> 00:03:31.000
share listed would be 50%.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:37.538
If you always offered same day shipping for the pitcher while no other seller offered this option,

00:03:37.538 --> 00:03:41.000
the same day shipping speed would also be 25.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:47.333
Cart adds is the number of times that customers used a query, clicked a product, then used the Add

00:03:47.333 --> 00:03:53.000
to Cart button on the product's detail page to put it in their cart for purchase later.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:59.577
Like with clicks, we provide a total count, brand count and brand share for cart adds as well as

00:03:59.577 --> 00:04:02.000
a column for same day shipping speed.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:08.577
We also provide a cart add rate, which is the percentage of time customers clicked the Add to Cart

00:04:08.577 --> 00:04:11.000
button after viewing a product detail page.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:18.385
For example, after clicking various products 50 times on Search Results pages for the query "water

00:04:18.385 --> 00:04:23.000
pitcher", customers added various products to their carts 30 times.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:29.926
If 10 of those products were your water pitcher, which was always the only product offered with

00:04:29.926 --> 00:04:34.000
same day shipping, the brand share listed would be 33.33%.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.000
And the same day shipping speed would be 10.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:43.387
If, in addition to the 10 cart adds, 10 other customers viewed your product detail page but didn't

00:04:43.387 --> 00:04:48.000
add the product to their cart, the cart add rate would be 50%.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:55.158
Finally, purchases is the number of times that customers used a query, clicked a product, then ordered

00:04:55.158 --> 00:04:56.000
the product.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:01.000
This metric includes your sales as well as the sales of other sellers.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:08.286
We provide a total count, purchase rate, brand count, brand share and same day shipping speed just

00:05:08.286 --> 00:05:10.000
like for cart adds.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:17.273
For example, after clicking various products 50 times on Search Results pages for the query "water

00:05:17.273 --> 00:05:20.000
pitcher", customers purchased products 20 times.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:26.080
If 5 of those products were your water pitcher, the brand share listed would be 25%, and the same

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:28.000
day shipping speed would be 5.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:35.192
If, in addition to the 5 purchases, 5 other customers viewed your product detail page but didn't

00:05:35.192 --> 00:05:39.000
purchase the product, the purchase rate would be 50%.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:45.538
Note that the metrics in the Search Query Performance Report are specific to Search and may not

00:05:45.538 --> 00:05:49.000
match metrics available in other Amazon reports and dashboards.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:55.000
That's because every report and dashboard defines and presents customer activity differently.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:02.367
When you first access the Search Query Performance Report, it'll be defaulted to show all the queries

00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:08.000
associated with your brand's products used by Amazon customers in the previous week.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:15.125
You can click "ASIN View" at the top of the report to view queries associated with a specific product

00:06:15.125 --> 00:06:17.000
instead of your entire brand.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:23.667
Use the search bar to find the product, select a specific time period using the drop-down menus,

00:06:23.667 --> 00:06:27.000
then click the "Apply" button to refresh the report.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:34.158
When selecting a time period, keep in mind that data is generally available in brand analytics within

00:06:34.158 --> 00:06:35.000
72 hours.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:42.200
Back on the "Brand View" section of the report, you can use the first drop-down menu to narrow the

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.000
report to a specific brand.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:48.000
You can also use the other two drop-down menus to view a specific time period.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:53.000
After making selections, click the "Apply" button to refresh the report.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:58.677
If you'd like to add or remove columns on the Search Query Performance Report, click "Customize

00:06:58.677 --> 00:07:04.000
Columns" on the right-hand side, then check or uncheck boxes in the pop-up.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:08.000
Click the "Save" button to return to the updated report.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:13.000
To download a copy of the report, click the "Generate Download" button.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:20.207
Then in the pop-up, select either "Simple View" to download the report you see on screen or select "

00:07:20.207 --> 00:07:24.000
Comprehensive View" to download the report with all relevant columns.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:30.667
Click the "Generate Download" button to start your download, which you can monitor by accessing

00:07:30.667 --> 00:07:32.000
the Download Manager.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:38.522
Finally, if you want more information about how a specific metric is calculated, click "Metrics

00:07:38.522 --> 00:07:42.000
Glossary" to see a set of comprehensive definitions.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:48.000
On the "Metrics Glossary" page, you can expand each section to see additional details.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:54.769
We encourage brands to use all the features and functionality of the Search Query Performance Report

00:07:54.769 --> 00:07:59.000
to gain insights into their performance in the Amazon Store.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:05.538
Use it to suggest updates to the keywords associated with your product detail pages or to decide

00:08:05.538 --> 00:08:09.000
which product detail pages to enhance with A+ content.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:16.714
You can also use the report to identify keywords for sponsored products ads and to spot trends and

00:08:16.714 --> 00:08:18.000
new product opportunities.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:22.000
This concludes our overview of the Search Query Performance Report.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:29.650
If you'd like step-by-step instructions for other brand analytics reports, see our series of modules

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:31.000
in Seller University.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:35.000
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon Store!
